\begin{abstract}
In this paper, we study several coloring problems on graphs from the viewpoint of parameterized
complexity. We show that \pe{} is fixed-parameter tractable ($\fpt$) parameterized by distance to clique. We show that \ec{} is $\fpt$ parameterized by the distance to threshold graphs. We also study the \lck{} and show that the problem is NP-complete on split graphs and it is $\fpt$ parameterized by solution size on split graphs. 
%\begin{enumerate}
